## Goal

Extend the working prototype so an existing Area can be edited and saved.

After Task 04, a user should be able to:

1. Load an existing Area.
2. Select it on the map.
3. Edit its polygon geometry.
4. Optionally change its name.
5. Save the changes.
6. See the updated Area on the map.
7. Refresh the browser and see the updated Area.
8. Have every successful update recorded as a new AreaVersion.
9. Receive a conflict response if attempting to update a stale version.

The implementation must follow the versioning and optimistic concurrency
model defined in DESIGN.md.

